Instruction: Read the segment of a merger agreement and answer the multiple-choice question by choosing the option that best characterizes the agreement.\nQuestion: Is \u201cfinancial point of view\u201d the sole consideration when determining whether an offer is superior?\nOption A: No\nOption B: Yes\n\nMerger Agreement: SECTION 8.4. Evaluation of Offers. <omitted> (b) The Company Board, in determining whether an Acquisition Proposal constitutes a Superior Proposal, shall consider, in addition to the financial terms, the following factors: (i) the likelihood of obtaining regulatory approvals, (ii) the strategic alignment with the Company's long-term business objectives, (iii) the potential impact on employees and management, and (iv) any other factors deemed relevant by the Company Board. The Company shall provide Parent with written notice of any determination that an Acquisition Proposal is a Superior Proposal and shall include a detailed explanation of the basis for such determination, including any non-financial factors considered. (Pages 48-49)
